  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting access of vulnerable women, men, boys, and girls to lifesaving GBV prevention, risk mitigation, and response services in Akobo, Canal/Pigi, Fangak, Leer, Mayendit, and Kapoeta East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide GBV services to vulnerable people in South Sudan. Through this project, UNFPA provides GBV case management and psychosocial support, establishes referral systems, raises awareness, supports reporting of GBV cases, provides cash-based assistance, distributes dignity kits, and conducts training for service providers. The project provides GBV services to 57,877 people, including 31,227 women, 23,952 children and 8,682 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
